            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/yv5/yosemite5_cxl_ddr4_board_vr_mps.json",
                    "line": 808,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "It isn't obvious what \"MF\" and \"VF\" are.  If this is an appropriate change to make, can we spell them out?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/yv5/yosemite5_cxl_ddr4_board_vr_mps.json",
                    "line": 808,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Why did we make this change?  The reason isn't reflected in the commit message.  Probably belongs in a separate commit.\n\nMake sure we give reasons why we're removing the \"DDR4\" vs \"DDR5\" identifiers."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/yv5/yosemite5_cxl_ddr4_board_vr_mps.json",
                    "line": 808,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Kevin Tung",
                        "email": "kevin.tung.openbmc@gmail.com",
                        "username": "kevintungquanta"
                    },
                    "message": "VF and MF refer to Maple_Falls and \"Maple Falls\" and \"Victoria Falls\".\n\nShould expand VF/MF to their full names for clarity, or keep the shorter form?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/yv5/yosemite5_cxl_ddr4_board_vr_mps.json",
                    "line": 808,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Kevin Tung",
                        "email": "kevin.tung.openbmc@gmail.com",
                        "username": "kevintungquanta"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi @patrick@stwcx.xyz, VF and MF refer to \"Maple Falls\" and \"Victoria Falls\", respectively. The naming was changed from DDR4/DDR5 to VF/MF to better align with the board names.\n\nShould expand VF/MF to their full names for clarity, or keep the shorter form?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/yv5/yosemite5_cxl_ddr4_board_vr_mps.json",
                    "line": 808,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Expand it please.  I prefer not to use acronyms that are not going to be remembered in 8 months."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/yv5/yosemite5_cxl_ddr4_board_vr_mps.json",
                    "line": 808,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Kevin Tung",
                        "email": "kevin.tung.openbmc@gmail.com",
                        "username": "kevintungquanta"
                    },
                    "message": "Added the reason for removing the DDR4/DDR5 identifiers to the commit message."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/yv5/yosemite5_cxl_ddr4_board_vr_mps.json",
                    "line": 808,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Kevin Tung",
                        "email": "kevin.tung.openbmc@gmail.com",
                        "username": "kevintungquanta"
                    },
                    "message": "Expanded. Thanks."
                }
            ],
